message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper."
title: "Combinators on the Battlefield: BCKW and SKI Reduction in Magic: The Gathering"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Davis
    given-names: "N. E."
    alias: Sigilante
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1131-8319"
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sigilante/paper-mtg-bckw"
keywords:
  - combinatory logic
  - BCKW
  - SKI
  - "Magic: The Gathering"
  - recreational mathematics
abstract: >-
  Terms of combinatory logic are encoded as forests of Aura permanents in
  Magic: The Gathering and reduced in normal order by three game actions
  (re-attach, copy, sacrifice) in a cooperative, not forced, model. Checked by
  simulation against a reference reducer; rules legality is a reading of the
  Comprehensive Rules of 6 November 2026 without judge confirmation.
